{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration reached the intended overlap: configuration index 5 was committed, transfer to node 2 was active during application, and the same leader remained in joint state after transfer timeout. It then observed identical captured protocol/storage state across ten reliable tick rounds. A fresh proposal triggered automatic exit.\n\nThe run later failed because the driver treated a response from a now-removed peer as fatal. I’ll retain that failure, correct the driver’s handling of the documented rejection, and submit a separate formal check. The comparison will test a repeatable fair cycle, not treat ten ticks as an exit deadline.\n"}}
